WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.480 --> 00:00:01.443
- We always like to end the show

00:00:01.443 --> 00:00:03.870
with a gem of inspiration
from social media.

00:00:03.870 --> 00:00:05.280
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:07.680
(brief transition music plays)

00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:11.160
This story starts 15 years
ago when a then-aspiring actor

00:00:11.160 --> 00:00:13.560
from Utah was visiting New York City.

00:00:13.560 --> 00:00:17.820
A complete stranger gave him
$200 to see a Broadway show.

00:00:17.820 --> 00:00:20.100
It's a moment that always stuck with him.

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:21.510
Cut to 2022,

00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:23.790
and Claybourne Elder is
now a successful actor

00:00:23.790 --> 00:00:24.720
in his own right.

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:26.370
Starring in Company on Broadway

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:29.160
and in one of my favorite
TV shows, The Gilded Age.

00:00:29.160 --> 00:00:31.740
And thanks to a little recent serendipity,

00:00:31.740 --> 00:00:33.570
he's now helping hundreds

00:00:33.570 --> 00:00:36.750
of total strangers see
Broadway shows for free.

00:00:36.750 --> 00:00:39.210
We have him on the line
right now watching on NBC 4

00:00:39.210 --> 00:00:40.530
New York at three.

00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:42.139
What's up Claybourne?

00:00:42.139 --> 00:00:44.540
(audience cheers)

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:46.303
- How are you? Thank you for having me.

00:00:46.303 --> 00:00:48.930
- Oh my God, it's so nice,
first of all to meet you.

00:00:48.930 --> 00:00:49.763
I love you.

00:00:49.763 --> 00:00:50.730
Um, it's great to meet you.

00:00:50.730 --> 00:00:52.050
But you only set out

00:00:52.050 --> 00:00:54.690
to give away one pair of tickets, right?

00:00:54.690 --> 00:00:55.523
- That's right.

00:00:55.523 --> 00:00:57.330
Yeah. It was late in 2021.

00:00:57.330 --> 00:00:58.710
I got sick with Covid and was

00:00:58.710 --> 00:01:00.540
out of my Broadway show for a few weeks.

00:01:00.540 --> 00:01:03.150
And when I came back I wanted
to do something to celebrate

00:01:03.150 --> 00:01:03.990
you know, coming back.

00:01:03.990 --> 00:01:07.470
So I posted on Instagram that
I was giving away two tickets

00:01:07.470 --> 00:01:09.960
to anyone who couldn't afford them.

00:01:09.960 --> 00:01:11.700
And you know, I'd never reconnected

00:01:11.700 --> 00:01:13.410
with the man who gave me the tickets

00:01:13.410 --> 00:01:15.000
or the money for the tickets years ago.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:17.130
But I kind of wanted to honor his kindness

00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:19.980
in some way and pay it forward.

00:01:19.980 --> 00:01:23.520
And, um. Pretty
immediately, things blew up

00:01:23.520 --> 00:01:26.010
and somebody leaked my Venmo account

00:01:26.010 --> 00:01:28.620
and people started sending
me money to buy more tickets

00:01:28.620 --> 00:01:30.150
from all over the place.

00:01:30.150 --> 00:01:31.830
Some people sent me a thousand dollars

00:01:31.830 --> 00:01:33.438
some people sent me $2.

00:01:33.438 --> 00:01:34.271
- Wow.

00:01:34.271 --> 00:01:35.790
- They just sent whatever they could.

00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:37.890
And instead of giving away two tickets,

00:01:37.890 --> 00:01:40.678
I gave away 68 tickets to
that first performance.

00:01:40.678 --> 00:01:41.511
(audience cheers)

00:01:41.511 --> 00:01:42.476
- Wow.

00:01:42.476 --> 00:01:44.487
- In what I'm now calling
City of Strangers.

00:01:44.487 --> 00:01:45.620
- That's so cool.

00:01:45.620 --> 00:01:48.570
So how big is City of Strangers now?

00:01:48.570 --> 00:01:51.210
- Well, we've given away 1600 tickets,

00:01:51.210 --> 00:01:54.000
valued at over $25,000.

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:55.320
And when I look back

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:58.560
at that man who gave me the
money all those years ago,

00:01:58.560 --> 00:02:02.130
his kindness really
made me a kinder person.

00:02:02.130 --> 00:02:02.970
And that's the kind

00:02:02.970 --> 00:02:05.730
of thing I'm hoping to
inspire in some way.

00:02:05.730 --> 00:02:06.563
- Yeah.

00:02:06.563 --> 00:02:07.396
- To...for people.

00:02:07.396 --> 00:02:08.597
And this is really crazy, but, um-

00:02:08.597 --> 00:02:10.593
(audience cheers) thank you.

00:02:11.760 --> 00:02:13.788
And this is really crazy, but he uh-

00:02:13.788 --> 00:02:16.860
I posted it, and it went
viral and because of that

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:18.330
somebody saw that picture

00:02:18.330 --> 00:02:21.480
and recognized him and reconnected us.

00:02:21.480 --> 00:02:22.313
- Wow.

00:02:22.313 --> 00:02:23.640
- So I got to reach out to him

00:02:23.640 --> 00:02:25.410
and tell him what he
did for me 15 years ago.

00:02:25.410 --> 00:02:26.818
- [Kelly] Aww, that's so cool.

00:02:26.818 --> 00:02:28.350
- And now we're friends
and we text all the time

00:02:28.350 --> 00:02:29.340
and we just sort of knew

00:02:29.340 --> 00:02:31.650
that we were supposed to
be in each other's lives.

00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:32.670
- That is so cool.

00:02:32.670 --> 00:02:34.230
I mean, you're changing so many lives

00:02:34.230 --> 00:02:35.220
and inspiring so many people.

00:02:35.220 --> 00:02:36.840
Cuz I remember, I was a sophomore

00:02:36.840 --> 00:02:38.850
on a scholarship with a choir program.

00:02:38.850 --> 00:02:39.810
I wouldn't have been able to afford it

00:02:39.810 --> 00:02:42.000
and because people paid
the money, I was able to go

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:44.310
and see the shows with
everybody from Texas.

00:02:44.310 --> 00:02:45.720
And seeing "Les Mis"

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:47.940
as a sophomore in high
school, like changed my life.

00:02:47.940 --> 00:02:48.990
It was so beautiful.

00:02:48.990 --> 00:02:50.880
And I was like, I wanna be on stage.

00:02:50.880 --> 00:02:52.770
And it was like the big thing
that that drove me to that.

00:02:52.770 --> 00:02:55.800
So you're helping inspire
so many future actors

00:02:55.800 --> 00:02:56.700
and singers out there.

00:02:56.700 --> 00:02:58.230
So that's really cool.

00:02:58.230 --> 00:02:59.637
Thank you so much, much Claybourne.

00:02:59.637 --> 00:03:01.710
I'm liking your post right now. All right?

00:03:01.710 --> 00:03:02.543
- Thank you.

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:06.600
- All right, so that's
not all. Our season-long

00:03:06.600 --> 00:03:09.000
partner, Pilot Pen,
makers of G2 the go-to pen

00:03:09.000 --> 00:03:11.400
of the Kelly Clarkson
Show, want to honor truly

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:13.570
unstoppable people and
kind people just like you.

00:03:13.570 --> 00:03:15.240
So they're gonna be writing City

00:03:15.240 --> 00:03:17.572
of Strangers a check
for a thousand dollars.

00:03:17.572 --> 00:03:19.500
(audience cheering)

00:03:19.500 --> 00:03:20.333
- Amazing.

00:03:21.750 --> 00:03:23.010
Thank you very much.

